yle":"note"},{"level":2,"text":"Dispatch Loop Detection","type":"heading","anchor":"Dispatch-Loop-Detection"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" warns if ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is called more than 100 times per debounce interval. This usually means "},{"code":"send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" isn’t using the snapshot pattern, causing cascading re-renders that trigger re-dispatches."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Reducer Weight","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Reducer-Weight"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducers run synchronously on the MainActor. Move O(n²) work into an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and dispatch the result back as an action.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Effect Threading","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Effect-Threading"},{"style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Effects run on Swift concurrency’s cooperative thread pool via ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task { @concurrent in }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Blocking calls (","type":"text"},{"code":"Process.waitUntilExit()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"DispatchSemaphore.wait()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Thread.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") hold threads hostage. If enough block, the pool starves and the MainActor freezes.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Important"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use async alternatives: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"terminationHandler"},{"text":" + continuation instead of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"waitUntilExit()"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead of ","type":"text"},{"code":"